<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns"><key id="k0" for="node" attr.name="kind" attr.type="string" /><key id="k1" for="node" attr.name="label" attr.type="string" /><key id="k2" for="edge" attr.name="relation" attr.type="string" /><graph id="FoundationsVIIReadiness" edgedefault="directed"><node id="ARC-H1"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Define how a theory's accessible domain is fixed at formation and the minimum lawful founding data.</data></node><node id="ARC-H10"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Classify mutually independent reasons a lawful join may fail.</data></node><node id="ARC-H11"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Certify that a strict join carries content not available from either parent or a mere product/common refinement.</data></node><node id="ARC-H12"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Require each parent record used in a join to be native or honestly bridged, with no fallback laundering.</data></node><node id="ARC-H13"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Price retention of both parents and the genuinely joint contribution, including possible economies or cross-costs.</data></node><node id="ARC-H14"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Attribute a closure rewrite to theorist, carrier, other theory, observer, environment, or mixed trigger.</data></node><node id="ARC-H15"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">State necessary and sufficient conditions for a system to carry and execute its own enabling operation.</data></node><node id="ARC-H16"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Reconcile and sharpen existing layer-birth classes before introducing a new classification.</data></node><node id="ARC-H17"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Give a typed transmission table for upward, downward, and peer interfaces.</data></node><node id="ARC-H18"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Classify loss, ambiguity, and nonfactorization when a parent projects to a child interface.</data></node><node id="ARC-H19"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Determine when certified content from one theory can lawfully become available to a peer without a join.</data></node><node id="ARC-H2"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Give a complete typed classification of admission mechanisms into a theory domain.</data></node><node id="ARC-H20"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Define the middle ground between mutual irrelevance and formation of a joint theory.</data></node><node id="ARC-H21"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Make certified mutual irrelevance or obstruction a positive scientific result.</data></node><node id="ARC-H22"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Give prospective commitment a certified temporal order and distinguish preregistration from retrospective fit.</data></node><node id="ARC-H23"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Define and measure route residue around cycles of theories.</data></node><node id="ARC-H24"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">State when distinct lawful admission routes produce the same domain state and when order matters.</data></node><node id="ARC-H25"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Test whether evidence-arrival or bracketing order changes a join certificate.</data></node><node id="ARC-H26"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Relate enlargement of access/probe families to dissolution and endogenous manufacture of needles.</data></node><node id="ARC-H27"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Treat prospective commitments as finite, budgeted probes rather than cost-free universal reservations.</data></node><node id="ARC-H28"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Define residuals left by inaccessible, unadmitted, expired, or failed access claims.</data></node><node id="ARC-H3"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Decide from a rule set or closure operator when no admissible first extension can occur without external provision.</data></node><node id="ARC-H4"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Prove an anti-smuggling law for access growth, adjacent to but stronger than No-Free-Distinction.</data></node><node id="ARC-H5"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Separate co-sourcing from shared access and from independent joining.</data></node><node id="ARC-H6"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Define preregistered, timestamped, priced prospective commitments that can lawfully admit later evidence.</data></node><node id="ARC-H7"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Specify lawful domain growth, expiry, revocation, retraction, and rollback.</data></node><node id="ARC-H8"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Relate founding-domain width to later reachability without equating wider with better.</data></node><node id="ARC-H9"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">State the minimum certified preconditions before a pair may enter the join calculus.</data></node><node id="ARC-LAB"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Build a finite Two-Theory World containing bootstrap, prospective commitment, genuine/obstructed joins, order effects, and nulls.</data></node><node id="ARC-NG1"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">No admissible first extension under a closed self-referential admission regime without an allowed seed/bridge.</data></node><node id="ARC-NG2"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Resemblance-only admission cannot certify an independent strict join and may saturate domains.</data></node><node id="ARC-NG3"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">A prediction cannot be discharged solely by an observation whose admission was defined retrospectively by that prediction.</data></node><node id="ARC-NG4"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Results proved under total lenses do not transfer automatically to partial, self-owned access domains.</data></node><node id="ARC-NONGOALS"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Preserve the wish list's exclusions: do not redo I–VI, universalize partial results, or derive empirical phenomena.</data></node><node id="ARC-S1"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Require an applicability/bridge certificate for every named law imported from another paper or layer.</data></node><node id="ARC-S2"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Require evidence that a sound mechanism can actually be reached or fired in the declared substrate.</data></node><node id="ARC-S3"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Define a privilege as an instrument-accessed particular the system cannot revise from within its declared operations.</data></node><node id="ARC-S4"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">State exactly what one negative, exhaustive negative, and closed-family negative can falsify.</data></node><node id="ARC-S5"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Judge implementations against normative specifications, not examples that may be incomplete or inconsistent.</data></node><node id="ARC-S6"><data key="k0">wishlist_atom</data><data key="k1">Separate lawfulness, non-vacuity, reachability, actual firing, and occurrence.</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0001"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">ANALOGY_ONLY_OR_DOMAIN_MAP_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0002"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">VALID_AFTER_ADDED_HYPOTHESES</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0003"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0004"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0005"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0006"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0007"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0008"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0010"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0011"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0013"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0014"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0015"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0016"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0017"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0018"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0019"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0020"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0021"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0022"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0023"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0024"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0025"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0026"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0027"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0028"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0029"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0030"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0031"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0032"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0033"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0034"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0035"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0036"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0037"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0038"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0039"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">UNKNOWN_REQUIRES_PROOF</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0040"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRED</data></node><node id="BR-CITE-0041"><data key="k0">typed_bridge</data><data key="k1">PARTIAL_BRIDGE_SCOPE_INHERITANCE_REQUIRE